{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xy6hCwW5Cr1H226PhmErj3","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"0e0255b872f08dabafe9414d623820272cd475be\",\"date\":\"2026-10-13T17:24:58+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6827: Forward onPersist and onRemove through ChainingInterceptor (#6637)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Forward onPersist and onRemove through ChainingInterceptor\\n\\nFixes #6636\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Fp7T1pGYEMrMVp1M7AW9Fg\\n\\n* Keep the outbox from enqueueing events about its own rows\\n\\nNow that onPersist reaches EventInterceptor, saving an OutboxEvent row\\npublishes a SaveDbEvent about that row. With an @OutboxEventListener\\nthat accepts it, such as one taking SaveDbEvent<?> or EntityEvent<?>,\\nOutboxEventInterceptor saved another OutboxEvent for it, and so on,\\nuntil the JVM ran out of heap on the first create or update.\\nOutboxEventInterceptor now ignores entity events whose entity is an\\nOutboxEvent.\\n\\nThe new ChainingInterceptor overrides are @since 3.0.0, because 2.9.x\\nbuilds against Hibernate 5.6, whose Interceptor has no onPersist or\\nonRemove.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Stop auditing OutboxEvent with Envers\\n\\nWith hibernate.integration.envers.enabled=true, Envers writes the audit\\nrow of each new or changed OutboxEvent just before the transaction\\ncommits, with persist(entityName, Map). The SaveDbEvent for that row has\\na HashMap as its entity, so the OutboxEvent check in\\nOutboxEventInterceptor let it through to a listener such as one taking\\nSaveDbEvent<?>. That saved another OutboxEvent, whose audit row came\\nnext, and so on, with each payload nesting the previous one. On H2 the\\ncommit ended in OutOfMemoryError. On MySQL it ended in \\\"Data too long\\nfor column 'payload'\\\", so logins and the outbox poller failed.\\n\\nOutboxEvent is no longer @Audited, as on 2.9.x.\\nEnversAuditTableInitializerDatabaseIT expected an audit table for every\\nentity with an @Audited superclass, but Envers does not audit\\nOutboxEvent through BaseOpenmrsObject's annotation, so the test now\\nchecks the entity's own annotation.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"41c5821a9b8b2d184207c8842e4c4331e02aaa7f\",\"date\":\"2026-10-05T21:27:50+03:00\",\"message\":\"Resolve module enum classes in StringEnumType (#6633)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Resolve module enum classes in StringEnumType\\n\\nFixes #6632\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Fp7T1pGYEMrMVp1M7AW9Fg\\n\\n* Document that modules map their enums with StringEnumType\\n\\nThe class Javadoc said to delete StringEnumType once Obs, ConceptName\\nand OrderSet move to annotations. Modules now map their own enums with\\nit, so say that instead.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ja9UqKCQ2eMd7FaYQ2ewqz\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"b64e0729cce60c40dffb75788c4b43937a6fc77e\",\"date\":\"2026-10-05T08:23:37-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6818: Context.closeSession() closes sessions it did not open (#6651)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"2c9b2ee0dd005f64fa543ca8228c51f57cb319c7\",\"date\":\"2026-10-02T10:15:07-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6810: Extend cluster-safety to RolePrivilegeCache (#6627)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"07e8ea06f244de96907581535d4eff8dadbd0004\",\"date\":\"2026-10-01T09:26:04-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6707: Implement full caching for Global Properties (#6598)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"f10e3fb9a645378ab6682c21d6be478bfdab6199\",\"date\":\"2026-09-21T16:28:21-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6721: Replace StackWalker with a thread-local guard in UserDAO (#6588)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"34bd26a8166d1277f83e4fdf1bda550ff8cc49a6\",\"date\":\"2026-09-14T22:26:34+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6686: Restore relevance weighting in patient search lost in the Hibernate Search 6 migration (#6430)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Tusha\",\"authorEmail\":\"mujuzimoses@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"6d787a1e60899e39377ce5011b298a188b3354c6\",\"date\":\"2026-08-25T13:54:55-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6780: Add a MariaDB option to the test container harness (#6474)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"(cherry picked from commit 5983a2b85e60caf1fdf7edaa8abc860d9f1dd17d)\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"ac1bd8778fc13247eb712a6cd7a949461cccdb6b\",\"date\":\"2026-08-25T07:58:28-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6662: Get unchanged password hashing working using Spring's interfaces (#6219)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"(cherry picked from commit d58b63501b7fedd1e6b02981262d73122b967621)\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Ian <ian.c.bacher@gmail.com>\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"4d222c6085bbe13f62be68908ad9c3abbaa75db1\",\"date\":\"2026-08-21T12:44:57-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6729:  Let batch loading engage on the identifier and concept search paths (#6420)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Rohith Gurram\",\"authorEmail\":\"89861100+Rocker810@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"2ce847744295132bbe5fb97f369fab714f09b309\",\"date\":\"2026-08-20T19:57:34+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6731: Add paging support to the obs retrieval API (#6410)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Ian <ian.c.bacher@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"jwnasambu\",\"authorEmail\":\"33891016+jwnasambu@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"1f6cc621cb7bf97dc4283b0c808f96373d90054f\",\"date\":\"2026-07-22T15:41:22-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6711: Batch-load search result pages (#6363)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"9e011e2c09db99fd5cae20821e203fe9cc5f036b\",\"date\":\"2026-07-21T23:50:01+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6681: Improve LocationSearchCriteria query performance with pagination (#6359)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"omeri innocent\",\"authorEmail\":\"innocentomeri08@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"b68355b3dd934c7d5be3708d6637dfae8f845ee5\",\"date\":\"2026-07-21T11:26:59-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6713: Switch to saner DaemonThread protection scheme (#6349)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"d992f1746c140dc2effaf78fc86443ac35309a3c\",\"date\":\"2026-07-20T23:48:04+03:00\",\"message\":\"Bind caller-supplied names as query parameters instead of concatenating (#6335)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Bind the program-attribute name as a query parameter\\n\\ngetPatientProgramAttributeByAttributeName assembled its native query by\\nconcatenating the attributeName argument straight into the SQL text. Bind\\nit as a named parameter (:attributeName) instead so the value is always\\nhandled as a literal attribute-type name and can never alter the query.\\nThe patient-id list stays inlined since those elements are ints.\\n\\nAdds a regression test that a name containing SQL control characters is\\nmatched literally and resolves no attribute type.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TpKNfxm3QjwUBDePEtFm2H\\n\\n* Bind the global-property name in FilterUtil.getGlobalPropertyValue\\n\\nReplace the concatenated global_property lookup with a PreparedStatement\\nso the property name is always treated as a literal value rather than\\nbeing spliced into the SQL text.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Add regression test for FilterUtil.getGlobalPropertyValue name binding\\n\\nGuards that the property name is matched literally: a name carrying SQL\\ncontrol characters resolves no property (returns null) instead of being\\ninterpreted as query text, which the earlier concatenated query allowed.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"c21a7cbfa2c9f67c1991372a343217e949e04f44\",\"date\":\"2026-07-17T18:15:32-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6683: Skip full-text search with drugs when a concept is provided (#6346)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"11489bdb02063ff8138f45803c336b7ef4635179\",\"date\":\"2026-07-17T08:26:55-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6687: Improve performance of searches using the search index (#6342)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"adec7344f655076c00cfa8ef033d998c2b8e1f5d\",\"date\":\"2026-07-14T22:28:41+02:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6516: Fix outbox/broker issues found in events/CDC sign-off (#6298)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* TRUNK-6516: Fix outbox/broker issues found in events/CDC sign-off (#6289)\\n\\nAddresses findings 1, 2, 4, 5, 7 from the sign-off issue:\\n\\n- Finding 1: OutboxEventRegistry now triggers scheduler when listeners are\\n  found, replacing the SmartInitializingSingleton in OutboxTaskSchedulerInitializer.\\n  Adds registerBean() so modules can register listeners at runtime.\\n- Finding 2: Use Context.loadClass() instead of Class.forName() in\\n  OutboxPollingTaskHandler so module-defined event types resolve correctly.\\n- Finding 4: Change outbox_event.payload and completed_listeners columns\\n  from TEXT to MEDIUMTEXT in both the update changelog and schema-only snapshot;\\n  align OutboxEvent entity columnDefinition to match.\\n- Finding 5: BrokerEventListenerFactory now rejects BrokerIncomingEvent<?>\\n  (wildcard/raw) at registration time with a clear error instead of silently\\n  wiring a consumer that dead-letters every message.\\n- Finding 7: Document on OpenmrsServiceEventAdvice that a synchronous\\n  @EventListener exception aborting the service call is intentional.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Fix getMaximumPropertyLength to treat MEDIUMTEXT/TEXT/CLOB as unbounded\\n\\nOnly LONGTEXT was special-cased to return Integer.MAX_VALUE; MEDIUMTEXT\\nand other LOB-like types fell through to column.getLength() (default 255),\\ncausing ValidateUtil to reject payloads that fit the actual DB column.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Fix tests broken by Finding 1 and Finding 5 refactors\\n\\n- OutboxEventIT: afterSingletonsInstantiated() renamed to schedule()\\n- BrokerEventListenerTest: raw BrokerIncomingEvent -> BrokerIncomingEvent<String>\\n  to comply with the new fail-fast check for wildcard types\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Fix two test failures caused by Finding 4 and Finding 5 fixes\\n\\n- BrokerEventListenerTest: publish BrokerIncomingEvent<String> with a\\n  payload so getResolvableType() resolves to the concrete generic type\\n  and Spring's listener type-matching accepts it against the\\n  BrokerIncomingEvent<String> method parameter.\\n- HibernateAdministrationDAO: scope the MEDIUMTEXT/LONGTEXT unbounded\\n  treatment to only those two explicit columnDefinition values; remove\\n  CLOB since @Lob fields without columnDefinition map to CLOB in H2,\\n  which would suppress the 64 KB TEXT length check in\\n  BaseAttributeTypeValidatorTest.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Revise BrokerIncomingEvent/OutgoingEvent header docs and fix test\\n\\n* Address PR review comments on #6298\\n\\n- Restore deleteScheduledTasks() in OutboxTaskSchedulerInitializer and call\\n  it from OutboxEventRegistry when disabled or no listeners found, so JobRunr\\n  jobs don't keep firing after the last listener module is uninstalled\\n- Drop registerBean(): ModuleUtil.refreshApplicationContext re-runs\\n  afterSingletonsInstantiated() on module start, so module listeners are\\n  picked up without any module-side call\\n- Add String payloads to all three BrokerEventListenerTest events so\\n  getResolvableType() resolves to BrokerIncomingEvent<String> and filter\\n  tests actually exercise the source/broker filter logic\\n- Add wildcard BrokerIncomingEvent<?> test case to BrokerEventListenerFactoryTest\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Rafal Korytkowski\",\"authorEmail\":\"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"84963803c794accceb19cf2236b859c747371336\",\"date\":\"2026-07-01T13:43:53+02:00\",\"message\":\"Fix @since 2.9.x to 2.9.0\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"rkorytkowski\",\"authorEmail\":\"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"c4aca3af4154dc99969cb6aed48a1e71c9a70055\",\"date\":\"2026-07-01T11:17:09+02:00\",\"message\":\"Porting TRUNK-6429 and TRUNK-6515 to master (#6233)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* TRUNK-6429: Create application events for service method calls and entity changes (#6084)\\n\\n(cherry picked from commit 144fee399f79b7152f2fcbaade069a7cfd3285e3)\\n\\n* TRUNK-6516: Provide CDC mechanism with Debezium (#6151)\\n\\n(cherry picked from commit 57f4018ffbcdb27dac86677ca2791d9fae6cfc89)\\n\\n* TRUNK-6429: Addressing post commit review (#6190)\\n\\n(cherry picked from commit a4331e297c2ad33b9d615174f7b6e52b26ef236c)\",\"authorName\":\"Rafal Korytkowski\",\"authorEmail\":\"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"b3a2fa0b2d45c31065f89651f4f9801aa45354b4\",\"date\":\"2026-06-01T17:21:50-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6633 Add a way to search Concepts by ConceptSearchCriteria, (#6079)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* TRUNK-6633 Add a way to search Concepts by ConceptSearchCriteria,\\n\\n* address feedback\\n\\n* add support for searching by concept name; fix test\\n\\n* address feedback\\n\\n* misc styling\\n\\n* change since version to 2.8.7; address feedback\\n\\n* add @BatchSize to ConceptReferenceTerm\\n\\n* switch to addUuids(String... uuids) and addConceptId(Integer... conceptIds)\",\"authorName\":\"chibongho\",\"authorEmail\":\"cbho@pih.org\"},{\"hash\":\"11607283d6100942c99bcdbb6713352f62c0b53a\",\"date\":\"2026-05-18T12:09:40-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6635 Add search by LocationSearchCriteria, with option to find … (#6088)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* TRUNK-6635 Add search by LocationSearchCriteria, with option to find descendent Locations efficiently\\n\\n* coderabbit suggestions\\n\\n* style\\n\\n* address feedback (with more efficient queries)\\n\\n* make LocationSearchCriteria take Location and LocationTag types instead of uuids\\n\\n* add @BatchSize to Location.tags to optimize location.getTags() calls\\n\\n* address feedback; change @since to 2.8.7\\n\\n* address feedback; change @since to 2.8.7\\n\\n* forward-port changes from #6089\",\"authorName\":\"chibongho\",\"authorEmail\":\"cbho@pih.org\"}],\"totalCount\":22}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"59bbebdc-1460-4fc7-9297-4fc44c73e081","uuid":"33fd5a5e-6976-4077-9062-f6a6f7109a44","timestamp":"2026-10-24T04:10:27.534Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"0e0255b872f08dabafe9414d623820272cd475be\",\"date\":\"2026-10-13T17:24:58+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6827: Forward onPersist and onRemove through ChainingInterceptor (#6637)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Forward onPersist and onRemove through ChainingInterceptor\\n\\nFixes #6636\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Fp7T1pGYEMrMVp1M7AW9Fg\\n\\n* Keep the outbox from enqueueing events about its own rows\\n\\nNow that onPersist reaches EventInterceptor, saving an OutboxEvent row\\npublishes a SaveDbEvent about that row. With an @OutboxEventListener\\nthat accepts it, such as one taking SaveDbEvent<?> or EntityEvent<?>,\\nOutboxEventInterceptor saved another OutboxEvent for it, and so on,\\nuntil the JVM ran out of heap on the first create or update.\\nOutboxEventInterceptor now ignores entity events whose entity is an\\nOutboxEvent.\\n\\nThe new ChainingInterceptor overrides are @since 3.0.0, because 2.9.x\\nbuilds against Hibernate 5.6, whose Interceptor has no onPersist or\\nonRemove.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Stop auditing OutboxEvent with Envers\\n\\nWith hibernate.integration.envers.enabled=true, Envers writes the audit\\nrow of each new or changed OutboxEvent just before the transaction\\ncommits, with persist(entityName, Map). The SaveDbEvent for that row has\\na HashMap as its entity, so the OutboxEvent check in\\nOutboxEventInterceptor let it through to a listener such as one taking\\nSaveDbEvent<?>. That saved another OutboxEvent, whose audit row came\\nnext, and so on, with each payload nesting the previous one. On H2 the\\ncommit ended in OutOfMemoryError. On MySQL it ended in \\\"Data too long\\nfor column 'payload'\\\", so logins and the outbox poller failed.\\n\\nOutboxEvent is no longer @Audited, as on 2.9.x.\\nEnversAuditTableInitializerDatabaseIT expected an audit table for every\\nentity with an @Audited superclass, but Envers does not audit\\nOutboxEvent through BaseOpenmrsObject's annotation, so the test now\\nchecks the entity's own annotation.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"41c5821a9b8b2d184207c8842e4c4331e02aaa7f\",\"date\":\"2026-10-05T21:27:50+03:00\",\"message\":\"Resolve module enum classes in StringEnumType (#6633)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Resolve module enum classes in StringEnumType\\n\\nFixes #6632\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Fp7T1pGYEMrMVp1M7AW9Fg\\n\\n* Document that modules map their enums with StringEnumType\\n\\nThe class Javadoc said to delete StringEnumType once Obs, ConceptName\\nand OrderSet move to annotations. Modules now map their own enums with\\nit, so say that instead.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ja9UqKCQ2eMd7FaYQ2ewqz\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"b64e0729cce60c40dffb75788c4b43937a6fc77e\",\"date\":\"2026-10-05T08:23:37-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6818: Context.closeSession() closes sessions it did not open (#6651)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"2c9b2ee0dd005f64fa543ca8228c51f57cb319c7\",\"date\":\"2026-10-02T10:15:07-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6810: Extend cluster-safety to RolePrivilegeCache (#6627)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"07e8ea06f244de96907581535d4eff8dadbd0004\",\"date\":\"2026-10-01T09:26:04-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6707: Implement full caching for Global Properties (#6598)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"f10e3fb9a645378ab6682c21d6be478bfdab6199\",\"date\":\"2026-09-21T16:28:21-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6721: Replace StackWalker with a thread-local guard in UserDAO (#6588)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"34bd26a8166d1277f83e4fdf1bda550ff8cc49a6\",\"date\":\"2026-09-14T22:26:34+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6686: Restore relevance weighting in patient search lost in the Hibernate Search 6 migration (#6430)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Tusha\",\"authorEmail\":\"mujuzimoses@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"6d787a1e60899e39377ce5011b298a188b3354c6\",\"date\":\"2026-08-25T13:54:55-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6780: Add a MariaDB option to the test container harness (#6474)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"(cherry picked from commit 5983a2b85e60caf1fdf7edaa8abc860d9f1dd17d)\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"ac1bd8778fc13247eb712a6cd7a949461cccdb6b\",\"date\":\"2026-08-25T07:58:28-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6662: Get unchanged password hashing working using Spring's interfaces (#6219)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"(cherry picked from commit d58b63501b7fedd1e6b02981262d73122b967621)\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Ian <ian.c.bacher@gmail.com>\\n\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"4d222c6085bbe13f62be68908ad9c3abbaa75db1\",\"date\":\"2026-08-21T12:44:57-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6729:  Let batch loading engage on the identifier and concept search paths (#6420)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Rohith Gurram\",\"authorEmail\":\"89861100+Rocker810@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"2ce847744295132bbe5fb97f369fab714f09b309\",\"date\":\"2026-08-20T19:57:34+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6731: Add paging support to the obs retrieval API (#6410)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Ian <ian.c.bacher@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"jwnasambu\",\"authorEmail\":\"33891016+jwnasambu@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"1f6cc621cb7bf97dc4283b0c808f96373d90054f\",\"date\":\"2026-07-22T15:41:22-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6711: Batch-load search result pages (#6363)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"9e011e2c09db99fd5cae20821e203fe9cc5f036b\",\"date\":\"2026-07-21T23:50:01+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6681: Improve LocationSearchCriteria query performance with pagination (#6359)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"omeri innocent\",\"authorEmail\":\"innocentomeri08@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"b68355b3dd934c7d5be3708d6637dfae8f845ee5\",\"date\":\"2026-07-21T11:26:59-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6713: Switch to saner DaemonThread protection scheme (#6349)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"d992f1746c140dc2effaf78fc86443ac35309a3c\",\"date\":\"2026-07-20T23:48:04+03:00\",\"message\":\"Bind caller-supplied names as query parameters instead of concatenating (#6335)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Bind the program-attribute name as a query parameter\\n\\ngetPatientProgramAttributeByAttributeName assembled its native query by\\nconcatenating the attributeName argument straight into the SQL text. Bind\\nit as a named parameter (:attributeName) instead so the value is always\\nhandled as a literal attribute-type name and can never alter the query.\\nThe patient-id list stays inlined since those elements are ints.\\n\\nAdds a regression test that a name containing SQL control characters is\\nmatched literally and resolves no attribute type.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TpKNfxm3QjwUBDePEtFm2H\\n\\n* Bind the global-property name in FilterUtil.getGlobalPropertyValue\\n\\nReplace the concatenated global_property lookup with a PreparedStatement\\nso the property name is always treated as a literal value rather than\\nbeing spliced into the SQL text.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Add regression test for FilterUtil.getGlobalPropertyValue name binding\\n\\nGuards that the property name is matched literally: a name carrying SQL\\ncontrol characters resolves no property (returns null) instead of being\\ninterpreted as query text, which the earlier concatenated query allowed.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"c21a7cbfa2c9f67c1991372a343217e949e04f44\",\"date\":\"2026-07-17T18:15:32-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6683: Skip full-text search with drugs when a concept is provided (#6346)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"11489bdb02063ff8138f45803c336b7ef4635179\",\"date\":\"2026-07-17T08:26:55-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6687: Improve performance of searches using the search index (#6342)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"adec7344f655076c00cfa8ef033d998c2b8e1f5d\",\"date\":\"2026-07-14T22:28:41+02:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6516: Fix outbox/broker issues found in events/CDC sign-off (#6298)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* TRUNK-6516: Fix outbox/broker issues found in events/CDC sign-off (#6289)\\n\\nAddresses findings 1, 2, 4, 5, 7 from the sign-off issue:\\n\\n- Finding 1: OutboxEventRegistry now triggers scheduler when listeners are\\n  found, replacing the SmartInitializingSingleton in OutboxTaskSchedulerInitializer.\\n  Adds registerBean() so modules can register listeners at runtime.\\n- Finding 2: Use Context.loadClass() instead of Class.forName() in\\n  OutboxPollingTaskHandler so module-defined event types resolve correctly.\\n- Finding 4: Change outbox_event.payload and completed_listeners columns\\n  from TEXT to MEDIUMTEXT in both the update changelog and schema-only snapshot;\\n  align OutboxEvent entity columnDefinition to match.\\n- Finding 5: BrokerEventListenerFactory now rejects BrokerIncomingEvent<?>\\n  (wildcard/raw) at registration time with a clear error instead of silently\\n  wiring a consumer that dead-letters every message.\\n- Finding 7: Document on OpenmrsServiceEventAdvice that a synchronous\\n  @EventListener exception aborting the service call is intentional.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Fix getMaximumPropertyLength to treat MEDIUMTEXT/TEXT/CLOB as unbounded\\n\\nOnly LONGTEXT was special-cased to return Integer.MAX_VALUE; MEDIUMTEXT\\nand other LOB-like types fell through to column.getLength() (default 255),\\ncausing ValidateUtil to reject payloads that fit the actual DB column.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Fix tests broken by Finding 1 and Finding 5 refactors\\n\\n- OutboxEventIT: afterSingletonsInstantiated() renamed to schedule()\\n- BrokerEventListenerTest: raw BrokerIncomingEvent -> BrokerIncomingEvent<String>\\n  to comply with the new fail-fast check for wildcard types\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Fix two test failures caused by Finding 4 and Finding 5 fixes\\n\\n- BrokerEventListenerTest: publish BrokerIncomingEvent<String> with a\\n  payload so getResolvableType() resolves to the concrete generic type\\n  and Spring's listener type-matching accepts it against the\\n  BrokerIncomingEvent<String> method parameter.\\n- HibernateAdministrationDAO: scope the MEDIUMTEXT/LONGTEXT unbounded\\n  treatment to only those two explicit columnDefinition values; remove\\n  CLOB since @Lob fields without columnDefinition map to CLOB in H2,\\n  which would suppress the 64 KB TEXT length check in\\n  BaseAttributeTypeValidatorTest.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* Revise BrokerIncomingEvent/OutgoingEvent header docs and fix test\\n\\n* Address PR review comments on #6298\\n\\n- Restore deleteScheduledTasks() in OutboxTaskSchedulerInitializer and call\\n  it from OutboxEventRegistry when disabled or no listeners found, so JobRunr\\n  jobs don't keep firing after the last listener module is uninstalled\\n- Drop registerBean(): ModuleUtil.refreshApplicationContext re-runs\\n  afterSingletonsInstantiated() on module start, so module listeners are\\n  picked up without any module-side call\\n- Add String payloads to all three BrokerEventListenerTest events so\\n  getResolvableType() resolves to BrokerIncomingEvent<String> and filter\\n  tests actually exercise the source/broker filter logic\\n- Add wildcard BrokerIncomingEvent<?> test case to BrokerEventListenerFactoryTest\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Rafal Korytkowski\",\"authorEmail\":\"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"84963803c794accceb19cf2236b859c747371336\",\"date\":\"2026-07-01T13:43:53+02:00\",\"message\":\"Fix @since 2.9.x to 2.9.0\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"rkorytkowski\",\"authorEmail\":\"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"c4aca3af4154dc99969cb6aed48a1e71c9a70055\",\"date\":\"2026-07-01T11:17:09+02:00\",\"message\":\"Porting TRUNK-6429 and TRUNK-6515 to master (#6233)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* TRUNK-6429: Create application events for service method calls and entity changes (#6084)\\n\\n(cherry picked from commit 144fee399f79b7152f2fcbaade069a7cfd3285e3)\\n\\n* TRUNK-6516: Provide CDC mechanism with Debezium (#6151)\\n\\n(cherry picked from commit 57f4018ffbcdb27dac86677ca2791d9fae6cfc89)\\n\\n* TRUNK-6429: Addressing post commit review (#6190)\\n\\n(cherry picked from commit a4331e297c2ad33b9d615174f7b6e52b26ef236c)\",\"authorName\":\"Rafal Korytkowski\",\"authorEmail\":\"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"b3a2fa0b2d45c31065f89651f4f9801aa45354b4\",\"date\":\"2026-06-01T17:21:50-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6633 Add a way to search Concepts by ConceptSearchCriteria, (#6079)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* TRUNK-6633 Add a way to search Concepts by ConceptSearchCriteria,\\n\\n* address feedback\\n\\n* add support for searching by concept name; fix test\\n\\n* address feedback\\n\\n* misc styling\\n\\n* change since version to 2.8.7; address feedback\\n\\n* add @BatchSize to ConceptReferenceTerm\\n\\n* switch to addUuids(String... uuids) and addConceptId(Integer... conceptIds)\",\"authorName\":\"chibongho\",\"authorEmail\":\"cbho@pih.org\"},{\"hash\":\"11607283d6100942c99bcdbb6713352f62c0b53a\",\"date\":\"2026-05-18T12:09:40-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6635 Add search by LocationSearchCriteria, with option to find … (#6088)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* TRUNK-6635 Add search by LocationSearchCriteria, with option to find descendent Locations efficiently\\n\\n* coderabbit suggestions\\n\\n* style\\n\\n* address feedback (with more efficient queries)\\n\\n* make LocationSearchCriteria take Location and LocationTag types instead of uuids\\n\\n* add @BatchSize to Location.tags to optimize location.getTags() calls\\n\\n* address feedback; change @since to 2.8.7\\n\\n* address feedback; change @since to 2.8.7\\n\\n* forward-port changes from #6089\",\"authorName\":\"chibongho\",\"authorEmail\":\"cbho@pih.org\"}],\"totalCount\":22}"}],"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Xy6hCwW5Cr1H226PhmErj3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
